=========================================================================
🚀 MODULE 5: FORM ELEMENTS & INPUT VALIDATIONS (DEEP DIVE)
=========================================================================
Description: User se data collect karna, GET vs POST methods ki security, 
aur bina JavaScript ke pure HTML5 engine se live validation lagana.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THE <form> ACTION & METHOD (Data Travel Ki Architecture)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
<form action="submit_data.php" method="POST">

* Action Attribute:
  Jab user form ke aakhir mein 'Submit' button dabayega, toh woh saara data 
  backend ke kis server file ya API address par jayega, woh rasta yahan 
  likha jata hai.

* Method Attribute (Data Bhejne Ka Rasta):
  Data ko backend tak transfer karne ke do main tareeqe hote hain:
  1. GET Method ──> Yeh saare data ko browser ke URL bar ke andar openly 
     dikha kar bhejta hai. Yeh passwords ya personal info ke liye bilkul 
     KHARAB hai kyunki privacy leak ho sakti hai. Iska use sirf search boxes 
     ya filter options ke liye kiya jata hai.
  2. POST Method ──> Yeh data ko request ki body ke andar piche se (hidden 
     tarike se) secure tarike se bhejta hai. Login credentials, passwords, 
     aur sensitive data ke liye hamesha POST use hota hai.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. POWERFUL HTML5 VALIDATION ATTRIBUTES (Bina JS Ki Security)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
HTML5 form sirf data collect nahi karte, balki browser ke level par hi user 
ko galat data enter karne se rokte hain:

* required:
  Is attribute ko input tag mein jod dene se woh field compulsory ho jaati hai. 
  User us dabbe ko khali chodh kar form submit nahi kar sakta.

* pattern (Regular Expression - Regex):
  Yeh sabse advanced validation hai! Agar aap chahte hain ki user sirf aur 
  sirf 10 digit ka mobile number hi dale (na 9 digit, na alphabet), toh aap 
  pattern lock set kar sakte hain:
  
  <input type="tel" pattern="[0-9]{10}" placeholder="10 Digit Number">
  [0-9] ka matlab sirf ginti, aur {10} ka matlab exact 10 akshar hone chahiye.

* min aur max (Range Controller):
  Numbers ya Dates par boundary limits lagane ke liye iska use hota hai. 
  Jaise agar user ki age sirf 18 se 60 saal ke beech honi chahiye:
  
  <input type="number" min="18" max="60" placeholder="Enter Age">

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. FULL VALIDATION FORM STRUCTURE (Reference Code)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Aapke master reference ke liye ek complete HTML5 validated form code:

<form action="/save-profile" method="POST">
    <!-- Required Text Input -->
    <label>Full Name:</label>
    <input type="text" required placeholder="Enter your name">

    <!-- Pattern Locked Phone Number -->
    <label>Mobile Number:</label>
    <input type="tel" pattern="[0-9]{10}" required placeholder="10 Digit Number">

    <!-- Min/Max Controlled Range -->
    <label>Age (18 to 60):</label>
    <input type="number" min="18" max="60" required>

    <!-- Submit Button -->
    <button type="submit">Submit Data</button>
</form>

